findings.body:
This PR updates `cli.js` to 2.8.2 but leaves `tauri` at 2.8.2, even though tauri itself moves to 2.8.3 here.

::code{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="1-8"}

The CLI reads this metadata to check and suggest tauri versions, so the released CLI would report a stale version.

::suggestion{file="crates/tauri-cli/metadata-v2.json" lines="6-6"}
  "tauri": "2.8.3",

A version-bump PR shouldn't change transitive dependency resolution. This one does: `colored` and two other packages switch from `windows-sys 0.48` to `0.59`, and one moves from `windows-targets 0.48.5` to `0.52.6`.

::diff{file="Cargo.lock" lines="1319-1323"}

These changes mix dependency changes into a release without review. They may also not match what the registry versions of those crates actually declare.
